aluminumsulfate@earthlink.net wrote:
> P.S. Does anyone in the audience know where I can find information on
> the Loglan-related conlang known as "Plan A"?

I believe that you are referring to "Plan B" (Loglan itself having been 
'Plan A').

http://www.rickharrison.com/language/plan_b.html
has the only published description that I know of

Plna B was developed by Jeff Prothero, who was one of the major people 
involved in making Loglan have a YACC-parsable machine grammar.  Jeff is 
also practically a co-founder of Lojban, since he helped finance the 
legal battle with JCB and provided much assistance on our getting our 
own YACC-grammar.

Jeff is a computer person and not a linguist, and his description shows 
that emphasis.
http://www.geocities.com/raredata/conlanghumor.txt
has several messages from conlang, one of which was linguist Jacques 
Guy's interpretation of the Plan B description from his (a linguist's) 
point of view, and proposes his own variation which he calls Cee (i.e 
Plan C).

